# graphify knowledge-graph output.
# KEPT:  GRAPH_REPORT.md, wiki/*.md  - the human-readable index, small, useful.
# DROPPED: graph.json (9.3 MB), graph.html, cache/  - all regenerated by one
#          `graphify <path>` run, no value in git history.
graphify-out/graph.json
graphify-out/merged-graph.json
graphify-out/graph.html
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/.graphify_*
graphify-out/cost.json
graphify-out/manifest.json
graphify-systems-out/graph.json
graphify-systems-out/cache/
graphify-systems-out/.graphify_*
research/graphify-out/graph.json
research/graphify-out/cache/

# next-scaffold output that is regenerable
next-env.d.ts
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# local data build artefacts (regenerate with npm run db:harvest / db:embed)
data/local/

# Curated seed catalogue and city manifests under data/cities/ are tracked ON
# PURPOSE. They are hand-curated source, not a derived cache: the output of the
# deterministic `gen-seed` pass, and the Definition of Done requires >=250
# records with provenance committed plus an offline demo snapshot so the demo
# never needs the network. Only derived artefacts inside a city dir are ignored.
data/cities/**/raw/
data/cities/**/derived/

# stray pre-existing symlinks in the skills dir (not project files)

# OSM harvest responses. Regenerated by `npm run db:harvest`; never a source
# of truth, and committing them would make a stale cache look like data.
data/cache/

# Capacitor / Android build output. The android/ project itself is source and IS
# committed; these are the parts Gradle regenerates on every build.
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
android/.idea/
android/captures/
android/app/release/
*.keystore
*.jks

# Over-the-air update bundles. Generated by `npm run update:ship` and uploaded to
# Capgo, never something to commit.
*.zip
